<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Mainland Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Lao Issara</h1><p class="st-meta">1945 CE – 1946 CE · capital Vientiane</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The 'Free Laos' nationalist government formed in 1945 to resist the return of French rule, and the seedbed of Lao independence politics.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the Japanese surrender, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phetsarath-ratanavongsa">Prince Phetsarath</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-luang-phrabang">Kingdom of Luang Phrabang</a>, declared the unification and independence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laos">Laos</a>. When King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sisavang-vong">Sisavang Vong</a> sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and dismissed him, Phetsarath's supporters formed the Lao Issara government in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-vientiane">Vientiane</a> in October 1945 and deposed the king.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The provisional government, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khammao-vilay">Khammao Vilay</a> as prime minister and princes <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/souvanna-phouma">Souvanna Phouma</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/souphanouvong">Souphanouvong</a> as ministers, had little money or army and relied on support from Vietnamese communities and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viet-minh">Viet Minh</a>. It adopted a constitution and briefly restored <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sisavang-vong">Sisavang Vong</a> as constitutional monarch in April 1946.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>French forces retook <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-vientiane">Vientiane</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-luang-phrabang">Luang Prabang</a> in April and May 1946, and the Lao Issara leaders fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bangkok">Bangkok</a>, forming a government in exile. It dissolved in 1949, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/souvanna-phouma">Souvanna Phouma</a> returning to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-laos">Kingdom of Laos</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/souphanouvong">Souphanouvong</a> founding the communist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pathet-lao">Pathet Lao</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/lao-issara.jpg" alt="Lao Issara" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: SKopp · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Laos.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1945 CE – 1946 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Vientiane</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Phetsarath, Khammao Vilay</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Theravada Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Lao</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/laos">Laos</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Provisional Government of Laos, Free Laos</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1946&amp;focus=lao-issara" aria-label="Lao Issara on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7464 1511 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lao Issara lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7784 1767L7784 1767"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7784 1767h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7784 1767h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7784 1767h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Vientiane. <a href="/atlas?year=1946&amp;focus=lao-issara">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
